            <ArticleTitle>P-TEFb: finding its ways to release promoter-proximally paused RNA Polymerase II.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>0</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1080/21541264.2017.1281864</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The release of a paused Pol II depends on the recruitment of P-TEFb. Recent studies showed that both active P-TEFb and inactive P-TEFb (7SK snRNP) can be recruited to the promoter regions of global genes by different mechanisms. Here, we summarize the recent advances on these distinct recruitment mechanisms.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
